      "ANNIE: You can be creeped out by that, I am.\nMAYA: You Catholic?\nBRIDGET: Fallen. I went to Immaculate Conception from kindergarten to eighth grade.\nANNIE: Maya wanted Frannie to go to Catholic school, but I put my foot down.",
      "MAYA: I wonder where Frannie is...\nBRIDGET: Hello.\nFRANCES: Hello.\nBRIDGET: Did I win?",
      "BRIDGET: Quiet.\nFRANCES: I apologize.",
      "MAYA: Do you know how to get to the park? I don't trust Frannie to guide you.\nFRANCES: I apologize!\nBRIDGET: I can look it up on my phone.\nMAYA: For snacks. No sugar.",
      "FRANCES: Can I have some money?\nBRIDGET: Your mom said no sugar.\nFRANCES: Please!\nBRIDGET: We can buy an apple or something on the way home."
    ]
